WEBVTT

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:13.707
Hiya!

00:00:14.777 --> 00:00:17.098
Don't worry. I got it
right where I want it!

00:00:18.315 --> 00:00:19.911
[Sonic yelling]

00:00:20.037 --> 00:00:22.638
Can you believe Amazon
is gonna deliver packages
with these things?

00:00:25.687 --> 00:00:28.327
This was a horrible plan!
What was I thinking?

00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:32.353
I'm gonna puke!

00:00:34.919 --> 00:00:36.379
[Sonic moaning]

00:00:36.487 --> 00:00:39.428
Come on!
We gotta get out of here.

00:00:39.987 --> 00:00:41.507
Oh, don't tell me
that's all you got!

00:00:41.688 --> 00:00:42.827
I'm just getting started!

00:00:43.087 --> 00:00:45.247
Let me know if you want to go
round two with the blue.

00:00:46.154 --> 00:00:49.259
[groans]
[engine starts, revs]

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:59.448
[tires screeching]

00:01:03.495 --> 00:01:04.752
[Robotnik groans]

00:01:04.857 --> 00:01:06.617
Doctor! Are you okay?

00:01:07.678 --> 00:01:09.397
I saw a guy race out of here
and thought--

00:01:09.397 --> 00:01:10.718
That you should
stop them?

00:01:12.218 --> 00:01:13.218
Open your mouth...

00:01:13.798 --> 00:01:15.857
and say you thought that you
should stop them.

00:01:16.077 --> 00:01:17.877
No, I thought that maybe
I should check

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:18.877
to see if you were okay--

00:01:18.977 --> 00:01:22.297
You know what's hard about being
the smartest person
in the world?

00:01:22.357 --> 00:01:25.656
Everyone else seems stupid.
Stupid, yes! Way to go!

00:01:25.817 --> 00:01:26.817
You got that one.

00:01:28.238 --> 00:01:32.097
Whatever this creature is,
it's our job to secure it,

00:01:32.698 --> 00:01:35.497
neutralize it,
uncover the source of its power.

00:01:36.338 --> 00:01:37.377
And if it resists,

00:01:38.718 --> 00:01:39.718
we take it apart...

00:01:40.917 --> 00:01:41.917
piece by piece.

00:01:43.678 --> 00:01:44.777
See what makes it tick.

00:01:46.437 --> 00:01:47.537
Stone?
Doctor?

00:01:48.017 --> 00:01:49.157
Call Optical Illusions.

00:01:50.117 --> 00:01:51.617
Tell them I need new frames.

00:01:52.917 --> 00:01:53.917
They know what kind I like.

00:01:54.817 --> 00:01:57.297
Oh, and bring that quill.

00:01:58.077 --> 00:01:59.077
Yes, Doctor.

00:02:02.917 --> 00:02:03.917
[Tom] All right, pal,

00:02:04.298 --> 00:02:05.957
you need to start talking
right now.

00:02:06.057 --> 00:02:08.477
Who are you? What are you?

00:02:08.718 --> 00:02:10.617
I'm a hedgehog!
I feel like that's obvious.

00:02:11.277 --> 00:02:13.797
And I'm in big trouble.
Oh, you'rein big trouble?

00:02:13.957 --> 00:02:16.557
You're not the one who punched
some sort of government
weirdo back there.

00:02:16.678 --> 00:02:19.236
You think youhave problems?
I lost my rings.

00:02:19.517 --> 00:02:20.777
Rings?
What are you talking about?

00:02:20.977 --> 00:02:23.337
Okay. Rings are how
all advanced cultures

00:02:23.337 --> 00:02:24.678
travel between worlds.

00:02:24.897 --> 00:02:27.417
And now mine are
on top of a pointy building

00:02:27.417 --> 00:02:29.957
I've only ever seen
on your skintight T-shirt.
Hey.

00:02:30.597 --> 00:02:32.777
So, I'd like you to take me
to San Francisco,

00:02:32.778 --> 00:02:34.877
so I can get back my rings
and use them

00:02:34.877 --> 00:02:36.017
to go to the mushroom planet.

00:02:37.937 --> 00:02:40.178
Mushroom planet.
Yes!

00:02:40.497 --> 00:02:41.497
Right.

00:02:45.317 --> 00:02:48.417
Okay, pal, out you go.
I'm sorry, what?

00:02:48.417 --> 00:02:50.417
Look, this is
the worst possible time

00:02:50.418 --> 00:02:51.918
for me to get myself
into trouble, okay?

00:02:52.218 --> 00:02:54.198
You asked me to save your life,
I saved your life.

00:02:54.477 --> 00:02:57.658
Now, please, go find your rings.
And your mushroom land.

00:02:57.997 --> 00:02:59.497
Hopefully I'm gonna wake up
in a hospital bed

00:02:59.497 --> 00:03:01.457
and the doctor's gonna tell me
that my colonoscopy

00:03:01.457 --> 00:03:03.718
was a big success, okay?
So goodbye.

00:03:03.718 --> 00:03:05.917
Okay. Goodbye.
Goodbye.

00:03:09.018 --> 00:03:12.138
Why aren't you leaving?
I don't know where
San Francisco is.

00:03:12.257 --> 00:03:13.257
It's west.
West?

00:03:13.378 --> 00:03:14.598
Straight shot, can't miss it.

00:03:14.658 --> 00:03:15.658
Fine. That's cool.

00:03:15.778 --> 00:03:17.398
I'm totally cool
saying goodbye now.

00:03:22.638 --> 00:03:26.317
So, as I crashed into the cold,
dark water of the Pacific,

00:03:26.938 --> 00:03:28.298
I realized a few things.

00:03:29.238 --> 00:03:31.078
A, I have no idea
where I'm going.

00:03:31.698 --> 00:03:33.478
B, saltwater stings.

00:03:34.138 --> 00:03:38.237
C, I shouldn't even be on
this planet right now, but I am.

00:03:38.437 --> 00:03:40.437
Why? Because you shot me!

00:03:40.598 --> 00:03:42.317
I know.
You shot me!

00:03:42.558 --> 00:03:43.897
All right, I heard you
the first time.

00:03:43.957 --> 00:03:46.618
You don't have to pile it on.
Good grief.

00:03:47.058 --> 00:03:49.277
I'm wet. I'm cold.

00:03:49.757 --> 00:03:51.178
There's a fish on my head!

00:03:51.178 --> 00:03:54.757
And clearly, I'm not gonna
be able to do this on my own.

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:02.067
[sighs] All right,
get in the truck.

00:04:02.187 --> 00:04:03.468
Really? You're gonna help me?

00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:06.627
I guess it is a little bit
my fault that all this
is happening to you.

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:10.387
Not a little bit. Entirely.
It is entirely your fault.

00:04:10.428 --> 00:04:11.627
Okay, it's entirely my fault.
Are you coming?

00:04:12.307 --> 00:04:13.307
Yes.

00:04:15.518 --> 00:04:17.318
Road trip! Whoop-whoop!

00:04:18.018 --> 00:04:19.018
[sighs]
What am I doing?

00:04:20.298 --> 00:04:22.098
[Tom] All right, there's
gonna be rules on this trip.

00:04:22.178 --> 00:04:24.958
Number one, do exactly
as I say all the time.

00:04:25.438 --> 00:04:27.138
Got it?
Got it, Donut Lord.

00:04:27.257 --> 00:04:28.778
Would you stop
with the "Donut Lord"?

00:04:29.498 --> 00:04:31.018
I have a name. It's Tom.

00:04:31.718 --> 00:04:32.718
I'm Sonic.

00:04:33.458 --> 00:04:35.798
Sonic. Sonic.

00:04:36.458 --> 00:04:38.737
So you've been
spying on us all for years.

00:04:38.958 --> 00:04:40.438
I wouldn't call it "spying."

00:04:40.738 --> 00:04:43.178
We were all just hanging out,
only I wasn't invited

00:04:43.178 --> 00:04:44.558
and no one knew I was there.

00:04:44.558 --> 00:04:47.358
I can't believe Crazy Carl
was right all this time.

00:04:47.378 --> 00:04:50.118
Yeah. You should call him
Super Observant Carl instead.

00:04:51.218 --> 00:04:53.238
Oh, my God,
stop the car right now!
What? What?

00:04:53.438 --> 00:04:55.818
[Sonic] The World's Largest
Rubberband Ball?

00:04:55.898 --> 00:04:57.718
We gotta see it!
No. No.

00:04:58.098 --> 00:05:00.318
No, this is not some
fun family road trip, okay?

00:05:00.578 --> 00:05:02.358
The government wants
to dissect you.

00:05:02.358 --> 00:05:04.438
And arrest me. This is serious.

00:05:05.958 --> 00:05:07.558
Eh, you're right, it was lame.

00:05:07.818 --> 00:05:09.738
Gift shop was cool, though.
I got you a mouse pad.

00:05:10.518 --> 00:05:11.538
When are we gonna get there?

00:05:11.818 --> 00:05:13.638
We will get there
when we get there.

